window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>In Chicago, justice wears no badge.</p> <p>The <i>Black Violet Agency</i> is all that stands between the city and the shadows swallowing it whole. Operating from a hidden office beneath the L train, three women carry on the legacy of a fallen founder—facing corruption, murder, and conspiracies so deep they’re practically fossilized.</p> <ul> <li>Brooke Navarro, the sharp-eyed tactician with a past she won’t share.</li> <li>Dakota Lane, the fearless infiltrator whose black lipstick hides a thousand scars.</li> <li>Allison Vega, the tech genius drowning in debt and coffee—but never out of ideas.</li> </ul> <p>When a murder reopens a case their founder died for, the team is pulled into a deadly spiral involving a secret organization, buried intelligence, and a ruthless assassin who knows their every move.</p> <p>As the city turns against them and the truth unravels, Brooke, Dakota, and Allison must rely on each other—and a few unlikely allies—to survive.</p> <p>But in the end, not everyone gets out.</p> <p>Tim Simpson delivers a dark, fast-paced thriller where loyalty is tested, trauma resurfaces, and justice isn't given—it's taken.</p>"; 
